    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><anchor id="index_1md__r_e_a_d_m_e"/></para>
<para>Real-time, on-device eye-gaze and 6-DoF head-pose tracking GDExtension for <bold>Godot 4</bold>, powered by <bold>ONNX Runtime</bold> and physical camera-to-display ray projection.</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
<sect1 id="index_1autotoc_md6">
<title>Key Features</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><bold>On-Device ML Pipeline (No External Services)</bold>: Runs face detection (<computeroutput>face_detection_yunet_2023mar.ort</computeroutput>), 35-point facial landmarks (<computeroutput>facial-landmarks-35-adas-0002.ort</computeroutput>), 3D gaze estimation (<computeroutput>gaze-estimation-adas-0002.ort</computeroutput>), and eye-openness classification (<computeroutput>open_closed_eye.ort</computeroutput>) locally via ONNX Runtime.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Physical Camera-to-Display Geometry</bold>: Solves 3D head pose via EPnP in millimeter camera space and intersects the fused gaze ray with the physical screen plane, converting automatically to Godot canvas and <computeroutput>CanvasItem</computeroutput>-local coordinates across window sizes and DPI scales.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>First-Class Godot Input Events</bold>: Dispatches <computeroutput>InputEventGaze</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>InputEventGazeMissing</computeroutput> through Godot&apos;s standard <computeroutput>Input</computeroutput> pipeline.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Reference-Counted Lifecycle (<computeroutput>GazeTracker</computeroutput>)</bold>: Automatically starts/stops camera capture and inference when nodes enter or leave the scene tree.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Inertial Dwell Node (<computeroutput>FillAccumulator</computeroutput>)</bold>: 2nd-order smooth dwell/charge accumulator with blink/micro-saccade momentum tolerance and distance-scaled off-target drain.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Mouse &amp; Gaze Coexistence</bold>: Built-in <computeroutput>MouseStillnessArbitrator</computeroutput> and bi-directional mouse emulation (<computeroutput>emulate_mouse_from_gaze</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>emulate_gaze_from_mouse</computeroutput>) so physical mouse input takes instant priority and mouse-only dev machines can test gaze UIs without a webcam.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Calibration &amp; Visual Debugger</bold>: Interactive <computeroutput>GazeCalibrationWizard</computeroutput>, persistent <computeroutput>GazeDeviceProfile</computeroutput>, and live <computeroutput>debug_cam_feed.tscn</computeroutput> camera overlay.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Headless CI Testing (<computeroutput>MockVisionServer</computeroutput>)</bold>: Deterministic synthetic camera/gaze driver for automated testing without hardware webcams.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Cross-Platform</bold>: Windows, macOS, Linux, Android, iOS, and Web (WebAssembly + <computeroutput>gaze_sidecar.js</computeroutput>).</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="index_1autotoc_md8">
<title>Installation</title><sect2 id="index_1autotoc_md9">
<title>Option 1: Prebuilt Release (<computeroutput>godot-gaze.zip</computeroutput>)</title><para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Download <computeroutput>godot-gaze.zip</computeroutput> from the <ulink url="../../releases">GitHub Releases</ulink> page.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Extract it into the root of your Godot project so that <computeroutput>addons/godot-gaze/</computeroutput> sits inside your <computeroutput>res://</computeroutput> directory (<computeroutput>res://addons/godot-gaze/gaze.gdextension</computeroutput>).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Open your project in Godot 4, go to <bold>Project -&gt; Project Settings -&gt; Plugins</bold>, and enable <bold>Godot Gaze</bold>.</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
</sect2>
<sect2 id="index_1autotoc_md10">
<title>Option 2: Building from Source (or Symlinking <computeroutput>project/addons/godot-gaze</computeroutput>)</title><para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Clone the repository with submodules (<computeroutput>thirdparty/godot-cpp</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>thirdparty/onnxruntime</computeroutput>): <programlisting filename=".bash"><codeline><highlight class="normal">git<sp/>clone<sp/>--recursive<sp/>https://github.com/browndragon/godot-gaze.git</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">cd<sp/>godot-gaze</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Download and prepare the <computeroutput>.ort</computeroutput> neural models into <computeroutput>project/addons/godot-gaze/models/</computeroutput>: <programlisting filename=".bash"><codeline><highlight class="normal">./scripts/download_models.sh</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Build the GDExtension for your platform (<computeroutput>macos</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>linux</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>windows</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>android</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>ios</computeroutput>, or <computeroutput>web</computeroutput>): <programlisting filename=".bash"><codeline><highlight class="normal">scons<sp/>platform=macos<sp/>target=editor</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">scons<sp/>platform=macos<sp/>target=template_debug</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">scons<sp/>platform=macos<sp/>target=template_release</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> <emphasis>(Optional)</emphasis> Regenerate Doxygen + Godot Editor Class Reference XML files (<computeroutput>project/docs/classref/*.xml</computeroutput>, loaded automatically in the editor from <computeroutput>res://docs/classref</computeroutput>): <programlisting filename=".bash"><codeline><highlight class="normal">./scripts/generate_docs.sh</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Symlink or copy <computeroutput>project/addons/godot-gaze</computeroutput> into <computeroutput>&lt;your-godot-project&gt;/addons/godot-gaze</computeroutput> and enable <bold>Godot Gaze</bold> in <bold>Project Settings -&gt; Plugins</bold>.</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect2>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="index_1autotoc_md12">
<title>Quick Start</title><sect2 id="index_1autotoc_md13">
<title>1. Lifecycle Management with <computeroutput>GazeTracker</computeroutput></title><para>By default, <computeroutput>gaze/general/autostart</computeroutput> is <computeroutput>true</computeroutput>, so tracking starts automatically on startup. For explicit scene-scoped tracking (or if you disable <computeroutput>autostart</computeroutput>), attach a <computeroutput>GazeTracker</computeroutput> node or call <computeroutput>GazeTracker.track_node(self)</computeroutput>. When all active <computeroutput>GazeTracker</computeroutput> nodes have <computeroutput>enabled = false</computeroutput> or exit the tree, <computeroutput>GazeServer</computeroutput> releases the camera automatically.</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".gdscript"><codeline><highlight class="normal">extends<sp/>Control</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">func<sp/>_ready()<sp/>-&gt;<sp/>void:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>#<sp/>Attach<sp/>a<sp/>reference-counted<sp/>GazeTracker<sp/>to<sp/>this<sp/>node&apos;s<sp/>lifetime</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>var<sp/>tracker<sp/>:=<sp/>GazeTracker.track_node(self)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>print(&quot;Tracking<sp/>active:<sp/>&quot;,<sp/>tracker.is_tracking_active())</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>print(&quot;Build:<sp/>&quot;,<sp/>GazeServer.get_build_info())<sp/>#<sp/>e.g.<sp/>&quot;godot-gaze<sp/>v0.1.0&quot;</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</sect2>
<sect2 id="index_1autotoc_md14">
<title>2. Handling <computeroutput>InputEventGaze</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>InputEventGazeMissing</computeroutput></title><para><computeroutput>InputEventGaze</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>InputEventGazeMissing</computeroutput> both inherit <computeroutput>InputEventGazeBase</computeroutput> (<computeroutput>InputEventAction</computeroutput>), so they flow through standard <computeroutput>_input(event)</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>_unhandled_input(event)</computeroutput> callbacks.</para>
<para><blockquote><para><bold>Important:</bold> Uninitialized or invalid gaze positions are represented as <computeroutput>Vector2(NAN, NAN)</computeroutput>, and clamping preserves non-finite values rather than collapsing them to <computeroutput>(0, 0)</computeroutput>. Always check <computeroutput>pos.is_finite()</computeroutput> before consuming gaze coordinates. </para>
</blockquote></para>
<para><programlisting filename=".gdscript"><codeline><highlight class="normal">extends<sp/>Control</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">@onready<sp/>var<sp/>reticle:<sp/>Control<sp/>=<sp/>$Reticle</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">func<sp/>_input(event:<sp/>InputEvent)<sp/>-&gt;<sp/>void:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>if<sp/>event<sp/>is<sp/>InputEventGaze:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>#<sp/>2D<sp/>canvas<sp/>coordinates<sp/>(or<sp/>pass<sp/>`self`<sp/>for<sp/>coordinates<sp/>local<sp/>to<sp/>this<sp/>Control)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>var<sp/>gaze_pos:<sp/>Vector2<sp/>=<sp/>event.get_eye_gaze(self,<sp/>InputEventGaze.CLAMPING_DEFAULT)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>if<sp/>gaze_pos.is_finite():</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>reticle.position<sp/>=<sp/>gaze_pos</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>reticle.visible<sp/>=<sp/>true</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>#<sp/>Optional<sp/>head<sp/>pose<sp/>projection<sp/>&amp;<sp/>continuous<sp/>eye<sp/>openness<sp/>[0.0<sp/>closed<sp/>..<sp/>1.0<sp/>open]</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>var<sp/>nose_pos:<sp/>Vector2<sp/>=<sp/>event.get_nose_gaze(self)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>var<sp/>left_open:<sp/>float<sp/>=<sp/>event.left_eye_openness</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>var<sp/>right_open:<sp/>float<sp/>=<sp/>event.right_eye_openness</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>#<sp/>3D<sp/>transforms<sp/>in<sp/>camera-space<sp/>millimeters</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>var<sp/>_head_xform:<sp/>Transform3D<sp/>=<sp/>event.head_transform</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>var<sp/>_gaze_xform:<sp/>Transform3D<sp/>=<sp/>event.gaze_transform</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>elif<sp/>event<sp/>is<sp/>InputEventGazeMissing:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>reticle.visible<sp/>=<sp/>false</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>match<sp/>event.reason:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>InputEventGazeMissing.REASON_NO_FACE_DETECTED:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>pass<sp/>#<sp/>No<sp/>face<sp/>in<sp/>camera<sp/>frame</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>InputEventGazeMissing.REASON_OCCLUDED:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>pass<sp/>#<sp/>Eyes<sp/>occluded<sp/>/<sp/>blink</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>InputEventGazeMissing.REASON_OUT_OF_BOUNDS:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>pass<sp/>#<sp/>Gaze<sp/>fell<sp/>outside<sp/>display<sp/>bounds</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>InputEventGazeMissing.REASON_SENSOR_INACTIVE:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>pass<sp/>#<sp/>Camera/pipeline<sp/>inactive</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><computeroutput>InputEventGaze.ClampingMode</computeroutput> options for <computeroutput>get_eye_gaze(local_to, clamping)</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>get_nose_gaze(local_to, clamping)</computeroutput>:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>InputEventGaze.CLAMPING_FREE</computeroutput> (<computeroutput>0</computeroutput>): Unclamped viewport/canvas coordinates (may fall outside the window).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>InputEventGaze.CLAMPING_CLAMPED</computeroutput> (<computeroutput>1</computeroutput>): Clamped to viewport bounds.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>InputEventGaze.CLAMPING_DEFAULT</computeroutput> (<computeroutput>2</computeroutput>): Uses the <computeroutput>gaze/pointing/default_clamping</computeroutput> project setting (default <computeroutput>true</computeroutput>).</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</sect2>
<sect2 id="index_1autotoc_md15">
<title>3. Inertial Dwell Interactions (<computeroutput>FillAccumulator</computeroutput>)</title><para><computeroutput>FillAccumulator</computeroutput> provides a 2nd-order damped charge/drain state machine for gaze buttons and dwell targets without harsh resets during blinks or micro-saccades:</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".gdscript"><codeline><highlight class="normal">extends<sp/>Control</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">var<sp/>dwell:<sp/>FillAccumulator</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">var<sp/>reticle_canvas_pos<sp/>:=<sp/>Vector2(NAN,<sp/>NAN)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">func<sp/>_ready()<sp/>-&gt;<sp/>void:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>dwell<sp/>=<sp/>FillAccumulator.new()</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>dwell.fill_sec<sp/>=<sp/>0.8</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>dwell.drain_sec<sp/>=<sp/>0.4</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>dwell.error_doubling_distance<sp/>=<sp/>100.0</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>dwell.process_callback<sp/>=<sp/>FillAccumulator.PROCESS_IDLE</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>dwell.filled.connect(_on_dwell_filled)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>add_child(dwell)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">func<sp/>_input(event:<sp/>InputEvent)<sp/>-&gt;<sp/>void:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>if<sp/>event<sp/>is<sp/>InputEventGaze:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>var<sp/>pos:<sp/>Vector2<sp/>=<sp/>event.get_eye_gaze()</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>if<sp/>pos.is_finite():</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>reticle_canvas_pos<sp/>=<sp/>pos</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">func<sp/>_process(_delta:<sp/>float)<sp/>-&gt;<sp/>void:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>if<sp/>not<sp/>reticle_canvas_pos.is_finite():</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>dwell.target_error<sp/>=<sp/>200.0</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>return</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>#<sp/>Signed<sp/>distance<sp/>outside<sp/>this<sp/>Control&apos;s<sp/>global<sp/>rect<sp/>(&lt;=<sp/>0<sp/>charges,<sp/>&gt;<sp/>0<sp/>drains)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>var<sp/>rect<sp/>:=<sp/>get_global_rect()</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>var<sp/>clamped<sp/>:=<sp/>reticle_canvas_pos.clamp(rect.position,<sp/>rect.end)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>dwell.target_error<sp/>=<sp/>reticle_canvas_pos.distance_to(clamped)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>queue_redraw()</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">func<sp/>_on_dwell_filled()<sp/>-&gt;<sp/>void:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>print(&quot;Activated<sp/>by<sp/>gaze<sp/>dwell!&quot;)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>dwell.reset()</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>You can also step manually with <computeroutput>dwell.process_callback = FillAccumulator.PROCESS_MANUAL</computeroutput> and call <computeroutput>dwell.process_error_delta(error_px, delta)</computeroutput> or <computeroutput>dwell.process_dwell_delta(is_active, delta)</computeroutput>. Signals emitted: <computeroutput>fill_changed(fill: float)</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>fill_started()</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>filled()</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>emptied()</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect2>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="index_1autotoc_md17">
<title>Mouse &amp; Gaze Coexistence</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><bold>Gaze -&gt; Mouse (<computeroutput>gaze/pointing/emulate_mouse_from_gaze</computeroutput>, default <computeroutput>true</computeroutput>)</bold>: Drives Godot&apos;s pointer position from gaze when the physical mouse is idle, with optional dwell clicks (<computeroutput>gaze/pointing/mouse_emulation_dwell_sec</computeroutput>, default <computeroutput>1.5</computeroutput>s). Moving the physical mouse outside the anchor bubble (<computeroutput>gaze/pointing/mouse_stillness_threshold_px</computeroutput>, default <computeroutput>3.0</computeroutput> px) immediately returns pointer authority to the mouse; remaining still for <computeroutput>gaze/pointing/mouse_stillness_duration_sec</computeroutput> (<computeroutput>1.5</computeroutput>s) blends control back to gaze over <computeroutput>gaze/pointing/mouse_emulation_transition_sec</computeroutput> (<computeroutput>0.3</computeroutput>s).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Mouse -&gt; Gaze (<computeroutput>gaze/pointing/emulate_gaze_from_mouse</computeroutput>, default <computeroutput>true</computeroutput>)</bold>: When no face/webcam feed is tracking, mouse movement synthesizes <computeroutput>InputEventGaze</computeroutput> events so you can develop and test gaze interactions with a regular mouse. Inspect runtime authority with <computeroutput>GazeServer.is_physical_mouse_still()</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>GazeServer.is_physical_mouse_active()</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>GazeServer.is_mouse_emulated()</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="index_1autotoc_md19">
<title>Customizing Events (<computeroutput>GazeEventFactory</computeroutput>)</title><para>To attach domain metadata or return a custom subclass of <computeroutput>InputEventGaze</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>InputEventGazeMissing</computeroutput>, extend <computeroutput>GazeEventFactory</computeroutput> and override <computeroutput>create_gaze_event()</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>create_missing_event(reason)</computeroutput>:</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".gdscript"><codeline><highlight class="normal">extends<sp/>GazeEventFactory</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">class<sp/>AppGazeEvent<sp/>extends<sp/>InputEventGaze:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>var<sp/>tag:<sp/>String<sp/>=<sp/>&quot;&quot;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">func<sp/>create_gaze_event()<sp/>-&gt;<sp/>InputEventGazeBase:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>var<sp/>base<sp/>:=<sp/>GazeServer.create_default_event()</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>var<sp/>ev<sp/>:=<sp/>AppGazeEvent.new()</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>ev.copy_from(base)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>ev.tag<sp/>=<sp/>&quot;gameplay&quot;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>return<sp/>ev</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">func<sp/>create_missing_event(reason:<sp/>int)<sp/>-&gt;<sp/>InputEventGazeBase:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>return<sp/>GazeServer.create_default_missing_event(reason)</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>Register your factory resource via <bold>Project Settings -&gt; <computeroutput>gaze/events/event_factory_path</computeroutput></bold> or dynamically via <computeroutput>GazeServer.set_event_factory(my_factory)</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="index_1autotoc_md21">
<title>Device Calibration &amp; Visual Debugging</title><sect2 id="index_1autotoc_md22">
<title>Device Profiles &amp; Interactive Calibration Wizard</title><para>Accurate projection relies on physical display pitch, resolution, and camera offset/tilt represented by <computeroutput>GazeDeviceProfile</computeroutput> (default storage path: <computeroutput>user://calibrations/device_profile.cfg</computeroutput> via <computeroutput>gaze/calibration/device_profile_path</computeroutput>).</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><bold>Built-in Wizard Scene</bold>: Instantiate <computeroutput>res://addons/godot-gaze/calibration/gaze_calibration_wizard.tscn</computeroutput> (<computeroutput>GazeCalibrationWizard</computeroutput>), connect <computeroutput>wizard_completed(profile)</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>wizard_canceled()</computeroutput>, and call <computeroutput>start_wizard()</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Programmatic Configuration</bold>: <programlisting filename=".gdscript"><codeline><highlight class="normal">var<sp/>profile<sp/>:=<sp/>GazeDeviceProfile.create_system_guess()</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">profile.camera_offset_mm<sp/>=<sp/>Vector3(0.0,<sp/>12.0,<sp/>0.0)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">profile.camera_tilt_deg<sp/>=<sp/>-4.0</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">GazeServer.set_device_profile(profile)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">profile.save_to_file(&quot;user://calibrations/device_profile.cfg&quot;)</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</sect2>
<sect2 id="index_1autotoc_md23">
<title>Camera &amp; Landmark Overlay (<computeroutput>debug_cam_feed.tscn</computeroutput>)</title><para>Instance <computeroutput>res://addons/godot-gaze/debug_cam_feed.tscn</computeroutput> (<computeroutput>DebugCamFeed</computeroutput>, configured by <computeroutput>gaze/debug/overlay_scene_path</computeroutput>) in your scene to visualize the live BGR camera preview, face bounding box, 35 facial landmarks, eye crops, and stage timings (<computeroutput>GazeServer.get_pipeline_stage_timings()</computeroutput>).</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect2>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="index_1autotoc_md25">
<title>Headless Testing &amp; CI (<computeroutput>MockVisionServer</computeroutput>)</title><para>The vision driver automatically switches to <computeroutput>MockVisionServer</computeroutput> when any of the following is true:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Godot is running headless (<computeroutput>DisplayServer</computeroutput> name is <computeroutput>"headless"</computeroutput>), e.g., <computeroutput>--headless</computeroutput> unit tests.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>--mock-camera</computeroutput> or <computeroutput>--mock-vision</computeroutput> is passed on the command line.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Environment variable <computeroutput>GAZE_VISION_DRIVER=mock</computeroutput> is set.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Project setting <computeroutput>gaze/vision/driver</computeroutput> is set to <computeroutput>"mock"</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>In tests, you can inject synthetic tracking state directly into <computeroutput>GazeServer</computeroutput>:</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".gdscript"><codeline><highlight class="normal">GazeServer.set_face_pose(Vector3(0.0,<sp/>0.0,<sp/>500.0),<sp/>Vector3.ZERO,<sp/>true)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">GazeServer.set_gaze(Vector3(0.0,<sp/>0.0,<sp/>500.0),<sp/>Vector3(0.0,<sp/>0.0,<sp/>-1.0))</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">GazeServer.set_eye_openness(0.95,<sp/>0.95)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">GazeServer.trigger_process()</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="index_1autotoc_md27">
