<sect1 id="index_1autotoc_md29">
<title>Web Export Guidelines</title><para>When exporting a project to <bold>Web (HTML5 / WebAssembly)</bold>:</para>
<para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para><bold>Enable the Godot Gaze Editor Plugin</bold>: Activating the plugin registers <computeroutput>GodotGazeExportPlugin</computeroutput>, which automatically copies <computeroutput>res://addons/godot-gaze/bin/gaze_sidecar.js</computeroutput> into your export output folder alongside the HTML/JS bundle.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Thread Support &amp; Cross-Origin Isolation Headers</bold>:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>If you enable <bold>Thread Support</bold> in your Godot Web export preset, browsers require <computeroutput>SharedArrayBuffer</computeroutput> cross-origin isolation. Your web server <bold>must</bold> send: <programlisting filename=".http"><codeline><highlight class="normal">Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy:<sp/>same-origin</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy:<sp/>require-corp</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>If your static host does not let you configure custom HTTP headers, <bold>disable Thread Support</bold> in the Web export preset so Godot uses the single-threaded <computeroutput>.wasm</computeroutput> GDExtension binary.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Web Model Assets</bold>: Web exports initialize <computeroutput>gaze_sidecar.js</computeroutput> (<computeroutput>onnxruntime-web</computeroutput>) against <computeroutput>res://models/face_detection_yunet_2023mar.onnx</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>res://models/gaze-estimation-adas-0002.onnx</computeroutput>. Ensure those non-resource model files are included in your Web export preset&apos;s non-resource file filter (<computeroutput>*.onnx, *.ort</computeroutput>).</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
